 ```
+
+## 🐧 Linux
+
+```bash
+sudo apt install clang cmake ninja-build pkg-config libgtk-3-dev liblzma-dev   # build deps (Debian/Ubuntu)
+./tools/setup_linux.sh      # flutter create --platforms=linux (if missing) + downloads the Aether core into linux/aether/
+flutter run -d linux        # development
+./tools/package_linux.sh    # release: dist/rahvpn-linux-<arch>.tar.gz  (run with ./rahvpn/rah_app)
+```
+
+- On Linux the app runs the Aether core as a child process and exposes **SOCKS5 at `127.0.0.1:1819`** (Psiphon also HTTP at `127.0.0.1:1820`). There is no system-wide tunnel: a tun device needs root. Point your browser/apps (or the system proxy) at the SOCKS5 address.
+- Config, WARP identity and Psiphon data live in `~/.local/share/rahvpn` (or `$XDG_DATA_HOME/rahvpn`).
+- Firebase/FCM is Android-only and is skipped on Linux.
+- `RAH_AETHER_DIR=/path` overrides where `aether` and `pt/psiphon-tunnel-core` are looked up.
